#1268 KS-1318 + KS-1142 + KS-1316 (T2, a CHECKER). KS-1318: the combined default-shapes control goes from toHaveLength(3) to toEqual of the three tags in source order — RED PROOF (mandatory): ARM A (`return shapes.slice().sort()`) -> the combined cell ALONE red with the new assertion, 0 red with the old; ARM B (the `export default function` branch emitting another tag) -> 2 red new, 1 red old (the combined cell stayed GREEN under the old — the finding verbatim). KS-1142: K1's 27-package literal hoisted; the new K1b reads ks781's CORPUS from SOURCE TEXT and asserts its package set is a SUBSET of K1's (SUBSET-NOT-EQUAL: the cell says why subset, not equality — grade the reason: CORPUS is a FILE list, K1 a PACKAGE list, services/blockchain and services/shared guarded by K1 alone) — RED PROOF: swap one CORPUS path's package for one K1 does not list -> K1b reds; rename the CORPUS symbol so the parse finds nothing -> K1b reds (both sides assert non-empty first: [] is a subset of everything); restored -> 0 red. K1b READS SOURCE TEXT: apply Seat L7's own lesson ("any check that reads source TEXT for a setting is satisfied by that setting commented out") — plant CORPUS commented out / a second `const CORPUS` in a comment / a CORPUS split across lines, and grade each reading. KS-1316: the walk no longer descends into an uninvoked nested function expression — W9 (guard in an uninvoked nested arrow -> guarded false, was true), W10 (invoked by name -> true), W11 (IIFE, a PARENTHESIZED callee -> true), W12 (handed to a call -> true), W13 (a guard in a branch that never runs -> true, STILL NOT DECIDED and pinned as such: W13-UNDECIDED, declared scope). RED PROOF: under develop's walk with the cells present, exactly ONE red (W9), every control green at both ends. LEGITIMATE SHAPES for the walk (COMMISSION.md table): an arrow assigned to a const and called later in the continuation; a function DECLARATION (not an expression) nested and called; `.call`/`.apply`/`.bind(...)()`; an arrow returned and invoked by the caller; `await (async () => guard())()`; an optional call `fn?.()` — measure each through the real walk and say which it reads. KS1329-TSC: Seat L7 filed KS-1329 (Backlog) — packages/shared does not type-check src/__tests__, hiding 10 errors, "the three ks781 errors marked "after #1268 merges"" — run tsc with the test files IN the program at develop and at #1268's head, diff the finding sets, and name the three; a TS error INTRODUCED by #1268 in a file no CI leg type-checks is a finding (non-blocking unless it hides a wrong assertion — say which). NO-REFS-LINE: #1268's body carries no `Refs` line (gh_read_1.out) and names KS-1143 (a foreign key) — the squash body's key set must be exactly KS-1318, KS-1142, KS-1316 (MG-3).

